+    "looked_in": "looked_in lists the tiers looked in, in the request's lookup order: lookup_order, without short-term when the request names no issue.",
+    "nothing_found": "answered_by null (nothing found) is allowed only after every tier of the request's lookup order was looked in, or just the asked tier when tier is given. Anything else is a silent skip.",
+    "first_answer_stops": "Without every_tier, answered_by is the last tier in looked_in.",
+    "results_from_looked_in": "Every hit and match comes from a tier in looked_in; without every_tier, only from answered_by.",
+    "fingerprint_is_the_text": "A fingerprint is the sha256 of the exact text it travels with: read.text, a hit's text.",
+    "short_term_is_this_issue": "Every short-term path in an answer (a match, a hit, a read, a cite source, where a cite is stored) starts with '<issue>/', the request's issue.",
+    "update_matches_its_status": "waiting: no decision yet (decided_by, reply, decided_at and applied_version are null). approved or rejected: decided_by, reply and decided_at are set; applied_version is null. applied: decided_by, reply and decided_at are set; for Phoenix memory applied_version is the commit.",
